        "tag": "title",
        "text": "45"
      },
      {
        "y": 24.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 316.2,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "Economy and finance"
      },
      {
        "y": 71.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 455.2,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "In this unit we focus particularly on collocations (words that are often used together)."
      },
      {
        "y": 89.3,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 292.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "A International aid and development"
      },
      {
        "y": 117.6,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 480.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "European countries have, in recent years, turned their attention to supporting real and sustainable"
      },
      {
        "y": 127.5,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 509.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "development1 in Africa. There are many encouraging signs that such projects have taken root2. In the five"
      },
      {
        "y": 139.2,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 511.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "years up to 2015, a score of African countries achieved economic growth of more than 4% per year. Foreign"
      },
      {
        "y": 150,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 499.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "direct investment also rose. Africa’s share in world trade now shows real signs of recovering from a long"
      },
      {
        "y": 160.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 501.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "decline. From Ghana in the west to Ethiopia in the east and Mozambique in the south, Africa’s economies"
      },
      {
        "y": 171.8,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 512.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "have consistently grown more rapidly than those of almost any other region of the world. A dozen countries’"
      },
      {
        "y": 182.6,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 506.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "economies have expanded by more than 6% a year over a period of six or more years. But many millions of"
      },
      {
        "y": 192.3,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 507.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "people in Africa still live in deep poverty3 and more determined efforts are needed to tackle the problem."
      },
      {
        "y": 203.1,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 509.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The European Union is committed to supporting and allocating4 funds and development grants5 to those"
      },
      {
        "y": 213.9,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 505.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "African governments which are pursuing6 policies to reduce and eradicate7 poverty and improve access"
      },
      {
        "y": 225.6,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 298.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "to healthcare, education and clean water supplies."
      },
      {
        "y": 250.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 467.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 development which can continue over a long time 2 started to be accepted 3 abject poverty"
      },
      {
        "y": 261.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 472.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "is also a collocation 4 giving to be used for a particular purpose 5 money to help development"
      },
      {
        "y": 272.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 398.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "6 following policies is also a collocation 7 completely get rid of something bad"
      },
      {
        "y": 292.2,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 304.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Collocations related to the noun debt"
      },
      {
        "y": 310.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 238.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Countries often find it impossible"
      },
      {
        "y": 316.5,
        "x0": 322.1,
        "x1": 350.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "repay"
      },
      {
        "y": 319.3,
        "x0": 404.4,
        "x1": 440.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "burden"
      },
      {
        "y": 322.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 242.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "to repay debt; the debt burden is"
      },
      {
        "y": 334.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 245.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "too great. Easing the debt burden"
      },
      {
        "y": 346.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 234.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "or cancelling debt helps debtor"
      },
      {
        "y": 353,
        "x0": 277.6,
        "x1": 303.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "relief"
      },
      {
        "y": 357.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 394,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "countries/nations free themselves DEBT"
      },
      {
        "y": 361,
        "x0": 428.7,
        "x1": 451.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "ease"
      },
      {
        "y": 370.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 250.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "from the problem of incurring more"
      },
      {
        "y": 382.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 243.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "and more debt. Alleviating debt /"
      },
      {
        "y": 391.9,
        "x0": 268.1,
        "x1": 311.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "alleviate"
      },
      {
        "y": 394.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 254,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Debt relief for poor countries should"
      },
      {
        "y": 404.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 449.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "be a priority. cancel"
      },
      {
        "y": 423.2,
        "x0": 333.5,
        "x1": 359.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "incur"
      },
      {
        "y": 432.9,
        "x0": 75,
        "x1": 223.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "C Trade and cooperation"
      },
      {
        "y": 461.2,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 499.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Free trade agreements often cause disputes between countries, especially when one country thinks the"
      },
      {
        "y": 471.3,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 505.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "other is engaged in restrictive practices1. Occasionally, trade wars erupt, and sanctions2 or embargoes3"
      },
      {
        "y": 483.2,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 491,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "are imposed on countries that may not be lifted for long periods. On the other hand, countries closely"
      },
      {
        "y": 494.2,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 510.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "related economically and enjoying good relations have the possibility of entering into monetary union and"
      },
      {
        "y": 505.1,
        "x0": 109.2,
        "x1": 205.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "having a single currency."
      },
      {
        "y": 531.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 510,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 the placing of unfair restrictions, e.g. limiting imports 2 restrictions on what a country may import/export"
      },
      {
        "y": 542.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 313.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 total prohibitions on importing/exporting certain goods"
      },
      {
        "y": 558,
        "x0": 74.4,
        "x1": 214.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "D Economic difficulties"
      },
      {
        "y": 575.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 317.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "If an economy is badly affected by war, we may refer"
      },
      {
        "y": 578.8,
        "x0": 344.1,
        "x1": 452.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Common mistakes"
      },
      {
        "y": 587.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 302.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "to it as a war-torn economy. Economies in a bad"
      },
      {
        "y": 599.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 294.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "state are often referred to as ailing economies."
      },
      {
        "y": 603.2,
        "x0": 345.1,
        "x1": 505.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The verb meaning to reduce the value of"
      },
      {
        "y": 611.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 308,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Devaluation/Revaluation of the currency may be"
      },
      {
        "y": 615.2,
        "x0": 345.1,
        "x1": 507.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "a currency is to devalue (NOT devaluate)."
      },
      {
        "y": 623.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 302.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "necessary. [reduction/increase in value against other"
      },
      {
        "y": 635.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 304.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "currencies] Economies may go into recession and"
      },
      {
        "y": 647.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 500.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "not come out of / emerge from recession for several years. Indeed, countries may even suffer a"
      },
      {
        "y": 658.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 517.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "double-dip1 recession. A country may suffer from a slump in prices2 for its goods. Lower taxes may"
      },
      {
        "y": 670.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 355.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "be introduced to boost the economy3 when it is in recession."
      },
      {
        "y": 686.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 464,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 recession which ends and then begins again after a short time 2 serious fall/collapse in prices"
      },
      {
        "y": 698.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 189.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 give the economy a lift"
      }
    ],
