    "lines": [
      {
        "y": 69,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "45.1"
      },
      {
        "y": 71.5,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 468.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Try to remember the collocations in A opposite. Fill the gaps in these sentences."
      },
      {
        "y": 88,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 520.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 Development is important, but it should be development, not the kind that only"
      },
      {
        "y": 100,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 202.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "lasts a short time."
      },
      {
        "y": 112,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 451,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 The government is a policy of giving aid only where it is used to"
      },
      {
        "y": 124,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 307.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "poverty. (Give two answers for the first one.)"
      },
      {
        "y": 136,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 522.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 There have been some signs that development projects are root in"
      },
      {
        "y": 148,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 195,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "many countries."
      },
      {
        "y": 160,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 423.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 Millions of people still live in poverty. (Give two answers.)"
      },
      {
        "y": 172,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 422.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 The economy has from its decline and is now doing well."
      },
      {
        "y": 184,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 500.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "6 The struggle to economic growth in developing countries is a constant one."
      },
      {
        "y": 196,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 475.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "7 Governments often funds for specific overseas development projects."
      },
      {
        "y": 208,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 515.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "8 The goal should be to improve to better healthcare and education for the poor."
      },
      {
        "y": 224.3,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "45.2"
      },
      {
        "y": 226.9,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 506.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Rewrite these sentences about debt using more appropriate language from the opposite"
      },
      {
        "y": 238.9,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 284.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "page to replace the underlined words."
      },
      {
        "y": 255.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 473.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 Over a period of five years, the country got huge debts which it could not pay back."
      },
      {
        "y": 267.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 407.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 Countries in debt are completely at the mercy of wealthier nations."
      },
      {
        "y": 279.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 479.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 The weight of debt is so great in some countries that their economies are collapsing."
      },
      {
        "y": 291.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 525.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 Wealthier countries could do a lot to make the debt of poor countries less heavy, and indeed, in"
      },
      {
        "y": 303.3,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 461.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "some cases, could forget the debt altogether. (Give two answers for the first one.)"
      },
      {
        "y": 315.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 428,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 Over a period of three years, the country suffered a two-stage recession."
      },
      {
        "y": 327.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 424.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "6 The following year, there was a severe collapse in the price of crude oil."
      },
      {
        "y": 339.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 536.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "7 While some countries lowered the value of their currencies, one country alone increased the value"
      },
      {
        "y": 351.3,
        "x0": 127.6,
        "x1": 300.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "of its currency due to its strong economy."
      },
      {
        "y": 363.3,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 361.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "8 Urgent measures were needed to improve the economy."
      },
      {
        "y": 379.7,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "45.3"
      },
      {
        "y": 382.2,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 397.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Answer the questions using vocabulary from the opposite page."
      },
      {
        "y": 398.7,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 477.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "1 What kind of war can break out between countries concerning imports and exports?"
      },
      {
        "y": 410.7,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 534.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "2 Which two verbs are used with sanctions and embargoes to mean (a) ‘placing’ and (b) ‘removing’?"
      },
      {
        "y": 422.7,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 526.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "3 What is the name for activities which make free trade difficult or impossible between countries?"
      },
      {
        "y": 434.7,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 509.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "4 What kind of agreement is it when two or more countries decide to share a single currency?"
      },
      {
        "y": 446.7,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 488.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "5 What do we call sums of money given to poor regions to assist their economic growth?"
      },
      {
        "y": 458.7,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 407.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "6 What can we call an economy that is devastated by armed conflict?"
      },
      {
        "y": 470.7,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 524.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "7 What adjective beginning with the letter ‘a’ can be used to describe an economy in a bad state?"
      },
      {
        "y": 482.7,
        "x0": 116.2,
        "x1": 434,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "8 What noun can follow ‘debt’ to create a phrase meaning ‘removing debt’?"
      },
      {
        "y": 499,
        "x0": 78.5,
        "x1": 102,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "45.4"
      },
      {
